    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (3/3 passing, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization for owner creation, keeping each concern in its own small unit and reusing it everywhere addresses are handled.\n\n**New \u2014 `AddressNormalizer`** (utility, mirrors the existing `E164Telephone`/`Household` helpers): the single source of truth for the rule \u2014 trim, collapse inner whitespace, upper-case, then expand street-type abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`) token-by-token. `null`/all-whitespace normalize to `\"\"`.\n\n**New \u2014 `NormalizeOwnerAddress`** function step (mirrors `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`): mutates the request DTO's address in place so it is *stored and returned* normalized. Wired into `owners.POST.yml` right after validation and before the household checks.\n\n**Changed behaviour, reusing the normalizer rather than duplicating logic:**\n- `ValidateRequiredOwnerFields` \u2014 the `address` required-field accessor now checks `AddressNormalizer.normalize(...)`, so an address that is blank *after* normalization is rejected (400).\n- `Household.matches` / `Household.idFor` \u2014 address comparison and the shared household id now use `AddressNormalizer.normalize(...)` on both sides, so duplicate detection and the shared `householdId` compare the normalized form (robust even against non-normalized seed/legacy rows). Last-name canonicalization is left untouched.\n\nAll three new acceptance tests pass (whitespace/case, abbreviation expansion, blank-after-normalize rejection), and the full suite builds green.",
